@cc [owner:nareshshah139,label:infra] workspace-test-dependencies
In tests.yml, dependency setup MUST use one root npm ci for all workspaces and MUST NOT reinstall
individual workspaces afterward, so frontend and backend test tools remain available after the
shared-types build.

@cc [owner:nareshshah139,label:infra] generated-backend-test-client
In tests.yml, the backend Prisma client MUST be generated from the backend schema before the
backend tests run, so a clean dependency install exposes the schema's enums and client types.

@cc [owner:nareshshah139,label:verification] inventory-recovery-ci-coverage
Every pull request, regardless of target branch, MUST build all workspaces, run both full test
suites with the inventory recovery and API-boundary PostgreSQL gates enabled, and fail when executable state
presentations or recovery proofs fail.

@cc [owner:nareshshah139,label:verification] inventory-recovery-browser-gates
Recovery CI MUST run the interrupted-write and prior import/count browser scenarios against an
isolated loopback database and retain their diagnostics even when a scenario fails.

@cc [owner:nareshshah139,label:verification] pdf-regression-runtime
The full backend test job MUST provide pdftotext before running PDF regressions, so generated
PDF contents are validated without skipping or replacing the extraction assertions.

@cc [owner:nareshshah139,label:verification] invoice-recovery-formal-gate
Every pull request and main push MUST run the pinned invoice recovery model checker, verify
same-invoice recovery paths and negative controls, and retain diagnostics even on failure.

@cc [owner:nareshshah139,label:verification] invoice-recovery-tool-integrity
The invoice recovery workflow MUST verify the pinned TLA+ tool SHA-256 before executing it;
a failed download or digest mismatch MUST fail the job.

@cc [owner:nareshshah139,label:verification] contract-check-gate
Every pull request and main push MUST run npm run contracts:check on Node 24 after npm ci,
and fail when any @cc directive is malformed, duplicated or not attached to a declaration.

@cc [owner:nareshshah139,label:security;reliability] formal-checker-pinned-download
The invoice recovery formal verification workflow MUST verify the pinned SHA-256 of its
model checker after every download and fail if the artifact is unavailable or differs.

@cc [owner:nareshshah139,label:verification] appointment-overbooking-formal-gate
Every pull request and main push MUST run the pinned appointment overbooking model checker,
verify the booking limit at limits 1 to 3, and require each broken variant (no lock, count
outside the lock, ignored overbook flag) to fail as expected.

@cc [owner:nareshshah139,label:verification] appointment-calendars-formal-gate
Every pull request and main push MUST run the pinned appointment calendars model checker,
verify the Scheduled and Confirmed calendars at limits 1 and 2, and require each broken
variant (no target check, source-calendar count, count outside the lock, no compare-and-set,
no idempotent retry) to fail as expected.
